    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n78098" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρακαίω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έκαυσα</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>light</i> or <i>keep lighted
				beside</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ π. τοῖς νοσοῦσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.383d
				</span></i>
			; in ceremonies at tombs, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				2.415
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Macedonia</span>):—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάννυχος λύχνος π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					2.130
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of cautery,
				<i>burn partly</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν φλέβα παρακαύσῃς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Vid.Ac.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
